<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  OpenAMRobot 2.0 — hand-reviewed self-collision exemptions.

  Like robots/openarm/openarm.srdf, this SRDF exists ONLY to carry deliberate
  ACM exemptions into the MJCF collision lowering (`openral collision lower`,
  acm-only, source: mjcf). The sweep can auto-disable a pair only when it
  collides in EVERY sampled pose; these pairs do not, so each is a reviewed
  judgment recorded here instead of a hand edit to the generated ACM block.

  ARM ROWS: copied from robots/openarm/openarm.srdf (re-measured 2026-09-24,
  hazard-log Entry 045) with only the link names translated to this robot's
  URDF/TF names, because the arm collision_geometry is OpenArm's, copied
  byte-for-byte (see robot.yaml):
      openarm_{s}_finger_pair -> openarm_{s}_ee_link1
      openarm_{s}_link7       -> openarm_{s}_ee_base_link
  Every arm link frame (joint1..7, gripper, mimic finger) is identical between
  the two manifests, so the measured mesh clearances carry over unchanged.
  OpenArm's two torso rows (openarm_body_link0 vs the pedestals) have no
  counterpart: this robot has no OpenArm torso.

  NO rigid body rows. The carriage, adapter plate, arm profile, tablet, head
  light, head camera, column and chassis are rigid to each other and to the
  arm pedestals; any rigid pair that overlaps is always-colliding and the
  sweep disables it on its own, and one that does not overlap can never trip.
  A MOVING arm link (link1 .. ee_link2) is never exempted against any body
  part: those are exactly the contacts the kernel must stop.

  LIFT-INTERNAL ROWS (2026-11-04; re-measured 2026-11-11 on upstream's 8 Nov
  geometry, openamr-upperbody-sw #48 @ e6ab3d1). The only non-arm pairs that move
  relative to each other are carriage-side vs column-side parts; the second E-stop
  is now carriage-side (on the adapter plate). Measured with the kernel predicates
  on the committed boxes (tests/unit/_collision_kernel_verdict.kernel_link_gap)
  over lift_joint 0..0.35 m in 1 mm steps; every other carriage/column pair keeps
  >= 1.9 mm at every lift height and stays checked:
    lift_flag  vs stop_sensor_l1000   0.0 mm (contact), q 0.000-0.024
    lift_flag  vs stop_sensor_l1175   0.0 mm (contact), q 0.151-0.199
    lift_flag  vs stop_sensor_l1350   0.0 mm (contact), q 0.326-0.350
  The flag rides through each stop sensor's fork by design: that pass is how the
  lift senses 0 / 175 / 350 mm. Upstream's boxes for these parts are placeholders
  (`placeholder_*`), so the contact is not a mesh measurement. None of these links
  is an arm link, and every arm link vs each of them stays checked.
  Dropped on 2026-11-11 (now checked): adapter_plate vs column (the column's
  static profile ends 25 mm below the plate: 23.0 mm clear) and the flag rod vs
  every stop sensor (1.9 mm clear at every height).
  The lift_joint itself drives these pairs only; it is bounded by its own
  position limits [0, 0.35] and the kernel's joint-limit check, not by these.

  SAFETY (CLAUDE.md §3): every row here REDUCES what the kernel checks and
  needs safety-WG sign-off to change.
-->
<robot name="openamrobot_v2">
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_left_ee_link1" link2="openarm_left_link5" reason="OpenArm row (finger_pair/link5): meshes never closer than 16.3 mm (1500 certified poses); fitted primitives overlap at rest (d=-0.028 m)."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_right_ee_link1" link2="openarm_right_link5" reason="OpenArm row (finger_pair/link5): meshes never closer than 16.1 mm (1500 certified poses); fitted primitives overlap at rest (d=-0.028 m)."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_left_ee_link1" link2="openarm_left_link6" reason="OpenArm row (finger_pair/link6): meshes never closer than 23.8 mm (1500 certified poses); fitted primitives overlap in every pose."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_right_ee_link1" link2="openarm_right_link6" reason="OpenArm row (finger_pair/link6): meshes never closer than 23.8 mm (1500 certified poses); fitted primitives overlap in every pose."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_left_link5" link2="openarm_left_ee_base_link" reason="OpenArm row (link5/link7): wrist housings either side of link6, meshes never closer than 2.9 mm (1500 certified poses, 1st percentile 3.0 mm); fitted primitives overlap in 67%."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_right_link5" link2="openarm_right_ee_base_link" reason="OpenArm row (link5/link7): wrist housings either side of link6, meshes never closer than 2.9 mm (1500 certified poses, 1st percentile 3.0 mm); fitted primitives overlap in 69%."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="lift_flag_link" link2="lift_stop_sensor_l1000_link" reason="Lift-internal: the position flag rides through the 0 mm stop sensor's fork by design (placeholder boxes in contact, 0.0 mm, lift q 0.000-0.024 m); no arm link."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="lift_flag_link" link2="lift_stop_sensor_l1175_link" reason="Lift-internal: the position flag rides through the 175 mm stop sensor's fork by design (placeholder boxes in contact, 0.0 mm, lift q 0.151-0.199 m); no arm link."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="lift_flag_link" link2="lift_stop_sensor_l1350_link" reason="Lift-internal: the position flag rides through the 350 mm stop sensor's fork by design (placeholder boxes in contact, 0.0 mm, lift q 0.326-0.350 m); no arm link."/>
</robot>
